            <ArticleTitle>Cavitational bone defect: a diagnostic challenge.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>396-400</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with a history of trauma to the maxillary left anterior region presented with chronic pain of unknown etiology. Root canal therapy and periradicular surgery failed to resolve the persistent pain. A second surgical procedure revealed a bone cavity superior and distopalatally to the apex of the maxillary left lateral incisor. The suspected etiology was necrotic bone removed from the bone cavity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
